+
+### 12.3.5 Known associated format-lock extraction-structure failures (R07-C D-S)
+
+Extend the internal `LockReadIssue` vocabulary with `invalid_structure` for only
+the following decoded container and entry checks. They are a bounded extraction
+contract, not validation of the complete uv, Poetry, Pipenv or Conda lock format.
+Existing safe-read and caught decoder failures retain `unreadable` and
+`invalid_syntax` respectively and take precedence over these post-decode checks.
+
+| Captured format | Shape-compatible empty/missing values | Known structural failure |
+|---|---|---|
+| `uv.lock`, `poetry.lock` | Missing `package` key or an empty list | A present `package` value is not a list, or any list entry is not a mapping with a nonempty string `name` |
+| `Pipfile.lock` | Root mapping; missing `default`/`develop` sections or empty section mappings | Decoded root is not a mapping, or a present `default`/`develop` value is not a mapping |
+| `conda-lock.yml` | Decoded None (empty YAML or explicit top-level null); root mapping with a missing `package` key or empty list | Any other decoded root is not a mapping, a present `package` value is not a list, or any list entry is not a mapping with a nonempty string `name` |
+
+Present wrong-type values remain wrong-type even when falsey: do not coalesce
+`false`, zero, empty strings or empty mappings into a valid package list. A
+present null package collection or Pipfile section is invalid; this is distinct
+from an absent key. TOML has no decoded null. Keep the explicit legacy top-level
+Conda None exception; it is not evidence that every manager accepts that document.
+
+For list entry names, nonempty means the existing literal string value is not
+`""`; do not add name-spelling, version, build, hash or metadata validation.
+Whitespace-only or otherwise unsupported nonempty names retain existing capture
+and canonicalization behavior. Pipfile section keys and their associated values
+retain existing extraction behavior, including empty keys and opaque values; no
+new package-value schema is imposed here. Duplicate names and unsupported manager
+metadata remain governed by existing behavior. None does not certify those facts.
+
+Preserve the entire previously captured package set, including names from usable
+entries next to structurally invalid entries or from a usable Pipfile section next
+to a wrong-type section. Record `invalid_structure` as soon as any specified
+post-decode shape check fails. Preserve existing `unparsed` diagnostics exactly;
+the typed issue is not derived from warning text, and does not add raw content,
+new diagnostics or persisted fields. Do not retry or broaden content reads.
+
+Reuse §12.3.4's existing qualifying-origin association and per-package finding,
+message, fix hint, evidence order and paths for this third issue. Existing exact
+declarations and qualified package credit still win first, including a package
+already captured from a partially extracted associated lock. Only a remaining
+used package without that credit can become SKIPPED/INFO because a structurally
+failed captured lock is associated with an existing qualified use origin. No
+membership or pin credit is granted by SKIP. Python coverage is independent.
+Unassociated, wrong-manager, nearer-project or barrier-blocked locks retain
+existing outcomes. Keep D-F, D-L and the empty-result Python veto otherwise intact.
+
+Presence rules retain their existing artifact semantics. Mixed warnings,
+FAIL-only overrides, suppression, default text/export visibility and exit
+thresholds retain §12.3.4's contracts; the newly classified isolated WARNING or
+promoted CRITICAL can stop triggering exit 1. Full JSON retains SKIPPED findings.
+No rule ID, default severity, renderer, engine, scanner, persisted schema,
+dependency version, historical report or five-project gold is changed.
+
+This closes only these explicit decoded shapes. Other package-name grammar,
+package values/versions, manager format completeness, general dependency-manifest
+or requirements failures, omitted candidates/imports, listing and framework
+completeness, and broader sufficient certificates remain OPEN R07-C work.
 
